<title>SOUTH AFRICA: LEBOWA STRIKE THREAT SEEN AVERTED.</title>
<headline>LEBOWA STRIKE THREAT SEEN AVERTED.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo American Platinum Corp Ltd said on Saturday the threat of a strike at Lebowa Platinum Mines Ltd had been averted.</p>
<p>&quot;A settlement was reached and production has not been affected,&quot; a company statement said, without giving details of the settlement.</p>
<p>It said earlier that wage talks had deadlocked and the union had proceeded with a strike ballot.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
